# Collision cracks (docs/briefs/ice-glass.md, C138). Bodies of materials
# that crack meet the floor at different speeds, in the free space between
# the two ledges, thrown down from just over it so they land at about the
# speed they were thrown at: glass that shatters set down too gently to
# crack; the same glass thrown at 10 m/s, which always cracks, and then
# turns into powder; ice thrown at 5 m/s, just over the 50 cells per
# second from which a crack comes with a chance, and at 10 m/s; and glass
# that does not shatter dropped from 20 cells, landing at about 70 cells
# per second. Creative mode puts a block of ice in the air on the right;
# dug from below, it turns into a static body, and a wooden box thrown up
# into it at 20 m/s cracks it where it hits.
